  "rationale": "The plant G models the robot's motion and perception event possibilities in a small grid-world, allowing all five controllable actions and all four uncontrollable events. The specification E constrains the robot to prioritize forward exploration, only using move_backward in front-obstacle recovery, and reserves full_rotate for last-resort recovery after repeated failures. Directed turns are preferred for obstacle recovery, and the automaton ensures rapid return to forward progress after any recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model plant G with permissive transitions for all events, including all controllable actions from each perception state, and total transitions for all uncontrollable events.",
    "Specification E restricts move_backward to dedicated front-obstacle recovery, prefers rotate_clockwise for left obstacles and rotate_counterclockwise for right obstacles, and only allows full_rotate from a stuck state after repeated failures. All recovery actions are one-shot, and the automaton quickly returns to forward exploration when path_clear is observed."
  ],
